    "section": "Section 19-A",
    "sectionNo": "19-A",
    "chapterNo": 2,
    "chapterRoman": "II",
    "chapterName": "STAMP DUTIES",
    "title": "Payment of duty on certain instruments liable to be increased duty in Uttar Pradesh under clause (bb) of Section 3",
    "description": "19-A.Payment of duty on certain instruments liable to be increased duty in Uttar Pradesh under clause (bb) of Section 3\nWhere any instrument has become chargeable in any part of the States, other than the Uttar Pradesh, with duty under this Act, or under any other law for the time being in force, in any part of the States, and thereafter becomes chargeable with a higher rate of duty in the Uttar Pradesh under clause (bb) of the first proviso to section 3, then –\n(i) notwithstanding anything contained in the first proviso to section 3, the amount of duty chargeable on such instrument shall be the amount chargeable on it under Schedule I-A or Schedule I-B, less the amount of duty, if any, already paid on it in the States and;\n(ii) in addition to the stamps, if any, already affixed thereto, such instrument shall be stamped with the stamps necessary for the payment of the amount of duty chargeable on it under clause (i) in the same manner and at the same time and by the same persons as though such instrument were received in the States, for the first time, when it became chargeable with the higher duty.",
