    "section": "Section 55",
    "sectionNo": "55",
    "chapterNo": 5,
    "chapterRoman": "V",
    "chapterName": "ALLOWANCE FOR STAMPS IN CERTAIN CASES",
    "title": "Allowance on renewal of certain debentures",
    "description": "55.Allowance on renewal of certain debentures\nWhen any duly stamped debenture is renewed by the issue of a new debenture on the same terms, the Collector shall, upon application made within one month, repay to the person issuing such debenture, the value of the stamp on the original or on the new debenture, whichever shall be less:\nProvided that the original debenture is produced before the Collector and cancelled by him in such manner as the State Government may direct.\nExplanations. - A debenture shall be deemed to be renewed in the same terms within the meaning of this section notwithstanding the following charges: -\n(a) The issue of two or more debentures in place of one original debenture, the total amount secured being the same;\n(b) The issue of one debenture in place of two or more original debentures, the total amount secured being the same;\n(c) In the substitution of the name of the holder at the time of renewal for the name of the original holder; and\n(d) the alteration of the rate of interest or the dates of payment thereof.",
